{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801507509,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2814cbc0018wl4hcBdePTfLo","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","messageID":"msg_1e280c1e0001m6wZIbxPniyq6t","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-80fea31208f660cc","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Research Strategy - performance-5\"\ndescription: \"Lineage-local strategy for the performance lane of segment five: hook latency, turn caps and brief cost on the built state at HEAD 84de3d600fa.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"performance-5 strategy\"\n  - \"hook latency turn caps brief cost\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - performance-5\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nLineage `performance-5` of the segment-five fan-out in `009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research`. Lane: hook latency, turn caps and brief cost on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (HEAD `84de3d600fa`). Sibling lanes: `ux-5` (offer fit, decline and refusal safety, brief wording), `cross-cli-5` (per-runtime delivery and follow-through).\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nSegment five, command surfacing on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (HEAD 84de3d600fa): what still limits UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness. This lineage measures only the performance lane: advisor hook latency per prompt, the behaviour-runner turn caps that ended 41 turns in the phase 033 untuned arm, and the byte/token cost of the brief and of a started command.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] What does the advisor hook cost per prompt on the built state after phases 016 to 033, and does any measured path exceed its runtime's hook budget?\n- [ ] What ended the 41 capped turns in the phase 033 untuned arm, and can a runtime-keyed wall-clock cap reduce them without changing the measured outcome?\n- [ ] What does one brief cost in bytes and tokens on the built state, and which remaining byte is removable without losing the offer contract?\n- [ ] Does the pre-model hook and brief cost consume a measurable share of a behaviour-runner turn's wall clock, so that it competes with the turn cap?\n- [ ] Which latency instrument reports the built state's true p95, and which path does it still miss (cold first prompt, in-process plugin, Codex adapter)?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not re-running the before arm or any live behaviour arm; the phase 033 arena records are read, never regenerated.\n- Not measuring semantic routing quality (typed recall, false offers); segment four owns those floors.\n- Not editing the hook, the runner, the brief renderer or any tracked file. Read-only outside this lineage.\n- Not deciding offer wording or decline safety; that is the `ux-5` lane.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below, or 8 iterations.\n- Stop early if every remaining question needs a live arm, a build or a week of traffic that this read-only lane cannot create; record that as the honest bound.\n- Stop if a required source file is missing after three retries on the same path.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n\nIteration 1: re-measure the built-state hook cost from the committed health records and the phase 033 arena records, and separate hook wall time from arena wall time.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nSegment four (built state at `087888ec4a`, after phases 014 and 015) closed these performance numbers:\n\n- Hook duration over 1,828 records on 2026-11-13: median 178 ms, p95 294 ms, p99 396 ms, max 893 ms, none over 1,000 ms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:170]\n- Live brief on 44 typed rows: median 306 B, p95 337 B, max 350 B; head line median 88 B, p95 119 B, max 132 B; directive block 217 B, about 71 percent of a brief. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:167]\n- Segment four declined the in-process degraded scorer: 0 of 1,283 real records took the local scorer; worst composed path 568.2 ms against a 2.5 s budget. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:92]\n- Phase 033's untuned arm evidence adds: pooled gained 25, lost 15, p 0.0769 across 140 paired rows; opencode delivery unknown in both arms; 41 capped turns; sk-git rows that move HEAD cannot be measured by the runner. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt:1]\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Hook path: spec-kit shim -> advisor hook -> advisor CLI -> daemon; three Node starts on Claude.\n- Behaviour runner: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `CAP_MS` keyed by prompt kind (300,000 chat turn, 900,000 started turn) in segment four's reading.\n- Brief renderer: `runtime/lib/render.ts`.\n- Health records: `runtime/lib/metrics.ts` writes per-prompt rows including duration, brief bytes and degraded flags.\n- Phase 033 evidence: `033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt`, plus its session records.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-16T03:57:11.000Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: \\\"Deep Research Strategy - performance-5\\\"\\ndescription: \\\"Lineage-local strategy for the performance lane of segment five: hook latency, turn caps and brief cost on the built state at HEAD 84de3d600fa.\\\"\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"performance-5 strategy\\\"\\n  - \\\"hook latency turn caps brief cost\\\"\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - performance-5\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\nLineage `performance-5` of the segment-five fan-out in `009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research`. Lane: hook latency, turn caps and brief cost on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (HEAD `84de3d600fa`). Sibling lanes: `ux-5` (offer fit, decline and refusal safety, brief wording), `cross-cli-5` (per-runtime delivery and follow-through).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nSegment five, command surfacing on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (HEAD 84de3d600fa): what still limits UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness. This lineage measures only the performance lane: advisor hook latency per prompt, the behaviour-runner turn caps that ended 41 turns in the phase 033 untuned arm, and the byte/token cost of the brief and of a started command.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] What does the advisor hook cost per prompt on the built state after phases 016 to 033, and does any measured path exceed its runtime's hook budget?\\n- [ ] What ended the 41 capped turns in the phase 033 untuned arm, and can a runtime-keyed wall-clock cap reduce them without changing the measured outcome?\\n- [ ] What does one brief cost in bytes and tokens on the built state, and which remaining byte is removable without losing the offer contract?\\n- [ ] Does the pre-model hook and brief cost consume a measurable share of a behaviour-runner turn's wall clock, so that it competes with the turn cap?\\n- [ ] Which latency instrument reports the built state's true p95, and which path does it still miss (cold first prompt, in-process plugin, Codex adapter)?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Not re-running the before arm or any live behaviour arm; the phase 033 arena records are read, never regenerated.\\n- Not measuring semantic routing quality (typed recall, false offers); segment four owns those floors.\\n- Not editing the hook, the runner, the brief renderer or any tracked file. Read-only outside this lineage.\\n- Not deciding offer wording or decline safety; that is the `ux-5` lane.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below, or 8 iterations.\\n- Stop early if every remaining question needs a live arm, a build or a week of traffic that this read-only lane cannot create; record that as the honest bound.\\n- Stop if a required source file is missing after three retries on the same path.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\nIteration 1: re-measure the built-state hook cost from the committed health records and the phase 033 arena records, and separate hook wall time from arena wall time.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nSegment four (built state at `087888ec4a`, after phases 014 and 015) closed these performance numbers:\\n\\n- Hook duration over 1,828 records on 2026-11-13: median 178 ms, p95 294 ms, p99 396 ms, max 893 ms, none over 1,000 ms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:170]\\n- Live brief on 44 typed rows: median 306 B, p95 337 B, max 350 B; head line median 88 B, p95 119 B, max 132 B; directive block 217 B, about 71 percent of a brief. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:167]\\n- Segment four declined the in-process degraded scorer: 0 of 1,283 real records took the local scorer; worst composed path 568.2 ms against a 2.5 s budget. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md:92]\\n- Phase 033's untuned arm evidence adds: pooled gained 25, lost 15, p 0.0769 across 140 paired rows; opencode delivery unknown in both arms; 41 capped turns; sk-git rows that move HEAD cannot be measured by the runner. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt:1]\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Hook path: spec-kit shim -> advisor hook -> advisor CLI -> daemon; three Node starts on Claude.\\n- Behaviour runner: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `CAP_MS` keyed by prompt kind (300,000 chat turn, 900,000 started turn) in segment four's reading.\\n- Brief renderer: `runtime/lib/render.ts`.\\n- Health records: `runtime/lib/metrics.ts` writes per-prompt rows including duration, brief bytes and degraded flags.\\n- Phase 033 evidence: `033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt`, plus its session records.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-16T03:57:11.000Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801487036,"end":1794801507509}}}}
