{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801933087,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28815bd0029wf2YLFTZGHIvk","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","messageID":"msg_1e287fd6c001OFZIKKXo5nOLTI","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad307de2e3360c0e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5 && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/ANCHOR:answered-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -20; echo \"=== answered ===\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:answered-questions/,/MACHINE-OWNED: START/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -14; echo \"=== next focus ===\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/MACHINE-OWNED: END/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -12; echo \"=== state rows ===\"; jq -c 'select(.type==\"iteration\") | {iteration,status,newInfoRatio,findingsCount}' deep-research-state.jsonl"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] What does the advisor hook cost per prompt on the built state after phases 016 to 033, and does any measured path exceed its runtime's hook budget?\n- [ ] What ended the 41 capped turns in the phase 033 untuned arm, and can a runtime-keyed wall-clock cap reduce them without changing the measured outcome?\n- [x] What does one brief cost in bytes and tokens on the built state, and which remaining byte is removable without losing the offer contract?\n- [ ] Does the pre-model hook and brief cost consume a measurable share of a behaviour-runner turn's wall clock, so that it competes with the turn cap?\n- [ ] Which latency instrument reports the built state's true p95, and which path does it still miss (cold first prompt, in-process plugin, Codex adapter)?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not re-running the before arm or any live behaviour arm; the phase 033 arena records are read, never regenerated.\n- Not measuring semantic routing quality (typed recall, false offers); segment four owns those floors.\n- Not editing the hook, the runner, the brief renderer or any tracked file. Read-only outside this lineage.\n- Not deciding offer wording or decline safety; that is the `ux-5` lane.\n\n---\n=== answered ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n- What does the advisor hook cost per prompt on the built state after phases 016 to 033, and does any measured path exceed its runtime's hook budget?\n- What does one brief cost in bytes and tokens on the built state, and which remaining byte is removable without losing the offer contract?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n=== next focus ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: **The arena arm ran at an earlier commit than the dispatch brief's HEAD.** The five arenas were built at `b765c7a14c5`; HEAD is `84de3d600fa`, six commits later, all documentation and review commits. The arm's behavio...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n=== state rows ===\n{\"iteration\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.83,\"findingsCount\":null}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] What does the advisor hook cost per prompt on the built state after phases 016 to 033, and does any measured path exceed its runtime's hook budget?\n- [ ] What ended the 41 capped turns in the phase 033 untuned arm, and can a runtime-keyed wall-clock cap reduce them without changing the measured outcome?\n- [x] What does one brief cost in bytes and tokens on the built state, and which remaining byte is removable without losing the offer contract?\n- [ ] Does the pre-model hook and brief cost consume a measurable share of a behaviour-runner turn's wall clock, so that it competes with the turn cap?\n- [ ] Which latency instrument reports the built state's true p95, and which path does it still miss (cold first prompt, in-process plugin, Codex adapter)?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not re-running the before arm or any live behaviour arm; the phase 033 arena records are read, never regenerated.\n- Not measuring semantic routing quality (typed recall, false offers); segment four owns those floors.\n- Not editing the hook, the runner, the brief renderer or any tracked file. Read-only outside this lineage.\n- Not deciding offer wording or decline safety; that is the `ux-5` lane.\n\n---\n=== answered ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n- What does the advisor hook cost per prompt on the built state after phases 016 to 033, and does any measured path exceed its runtime's hook budget?\n- What does one brief cost in bytes and tokens on the built state, and which remaining byte is removable without losing the offer contract?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n=== next focus ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: **The arena arm ran at an earlier commit than the dispatch brief's HEAD.** The five arenas were built at `b765c7a14c5`; HEAD is `84de3d600fa`, six commits later, all documentation and review commits. The arm's behavio...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n=== state rows ===\n{\"iteration\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.83,\"findingsCount\":null}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5 && sed -n '/AN