{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802537300,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","part":{"partID":"prt_1e29141fb002I58lRv1nOnfisJ","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","messageID":"msg_1e2912a6e001nFjG6290gBo07f","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1bc802be20ebb1d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '100,130p' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts; echo \"=== 250 fallback callers ===\"; grep -rln \"skill-advisor-cli-fallback\" .skilled --include=*.ts | grep -v node_modules | head -6; echo \"=== spec 008 cold bounds ===\"; grep -n \"cold\\|271\\|277\\|2500\\|5000\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md | head -12"},"output":"  readonly ollamaName: string;\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// Cascade-probe timing constants. Each accepts an optional env-var\n// override so operators can tune the cascade without code edits. Defaults are\n// empirically tuned for the cascade reorder.\nfunction parsePositiveInt(value: string | undefined, fallback: number): number {\n  if (typeof value !== 'string') return fallback;\n  const parsed = Number.parseInt(value.trim(), 10);\n  return Number.isFinite(parsed) && parsed > 0 ? parsed : fallback;\n}\n\nconst DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = parsePositiveInt(\n  process.env.SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS,\n  2_500,\n);\nconst DEFAULT_LOCK_STALE_MS = parsePositiveInt(\n  process.env.SPECKIT_CASCADE_LOCK_STALE_MS,\n  30_000,\n);\nconst DEFAULT_SLEEP_MS = parsePositiveInt(\n  process.env.SPECKIT_CASCADE_SLEEP_MS,\n  25,\n);\nconst VOYAGE_MODEL = getCanonicalFallback('voyage');\nconst VOYAGE_DIM = 1024;\nconst OPENAI_MODEL = getCanonicalFallback('openai');\n=== 250 fallback callers ===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/ipc/socket-server.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/typed-command-routing.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts\n=== spec 008 cold bounds ===\n3:description: \"Meaning matching needs a local Ollama server with nomic-embed-text, yet no install document, doctor route or brief tells a user who installs Skilled into their own repository that it exists, what it costs or that it is off. This phase makes the state visible, adds one doctor route that plans the setup and waits for a yes, writes the cost into the install documents from a committed measurement script and defines the absent, cold and slow cases with tests.\"\n32:| **Handoff Criteria** | `/doctor:setup` names the embedder state, `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` plans the setup and writes nothing without a yes, the install documents state the measured cost and the absent, model-missing, cold and slow tests pass |\n42:**Scope Boundary**: What a person who installs Skilled into their own repository sees and does about the embedder that meaning matching needs. The state, one doctor route, the install documents, a committed measurement script and the behaviour when the embedder is absent, missing its model, cold or slow. Scoring, the meaning bar, the lane weight and the embedder choice stay as they are.\n53:- A deadline on the prompt embedding and tests for the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n65:A user who installs Skilled can see whether meaning matching is on, set it up through one doctor route that shows its cost before it acts, read that cost in the install documents and keep a working advisor when the embedder is absent, cold or slow.\n105:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:143:export const DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500;\n132:The operator's own first reading on the same Mac, reported in the dispatch brief and not rerun here because it needs the model unloaded: `ollama serve` idle at 46 MB resident, 421 MB in total with the model loaded, cold embedding calls of 271 to 277 ms over 3 calls and one advisor CLI call of 413 ms with the model cold. The phase replaces this reading with the output of the committed script (REQ-001).\n159:- **Model cold.** Nothing preloads the model. The first prompt after 5 idle minutes pays the load inside the 5,000 ms query deadline.\n160:- **Slow call.** The query deadline is `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000` (`system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts:110`), overridden only by `OLLAMA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` (`:124`). The Claude hook passes a budget of `DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500` (`hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:143`) and `.claude/settings.json:150` gives the hook 3 seconds. When the CLI child runs past its budget, `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` returns its fail-open result with reason `timeout` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:559`). So a server that accepts the connection and never answers costs the whole brief, not only meaning matching. This is read from the code and not reproduced, because reproducing it needs a hung server.\n172:- Commit `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, which records the model size, the resident memory of the server and its model runner, the loaded size, the keep-alive expiry, warm and cold embedding latency and advisor CLI latency as one JSON object. Without it no number in an install document can be reproduced.\n176:- Bound the prompt embedding with its own deadline of 750 ms, give a missing model and a timeout their own `disabledReason`, add a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning to a recommendation that ran without a prompt vector and test the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n211:| `ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` | Create | Absent, model-missing, cold, slow and warning cases |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  readonly ollamaName: string;\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// Cascade-probe timing constants. Each accepts an optional env-var\n// override so operators can tune the cascade without code edits. Defaults are\n// empirically tuned for the cascade reorder.\nfunction parsePositiveInt(value: string | undefined, fallback: number): number {\n  if (typeof value !== 'string') return fallback;\n  const parsed = Number.parseInt(value.trim(), 10);\n  return Number.isFinite(parsed) && parsed > 0 ? parsed : fallback;\n}\n\nconst DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = parsePositiveInt(\n  process.env.SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS,\n  2_500,\n);\nconst DEFAULT_LOCK_STALE_MS = parsePositiveInt(\n  process.env.SPECKIT_CASCADE_LOCK_STALE_MS,\n  30_000,\n);\nconst DEFAULT_SLEEP_MS = parsePositiveInt(\n  process.env.SPECKIT_CASCADE_SLEEP_MS,\n  25,\n);\nconst VOYAGE_MODEL = getCanonicalFallback('voyage');\nconst VOYAGE_DIM = 1024;\nconst OPENAI_MODEL = getCanonicalFallback('openai');\n=== 250 fallback callers ===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/ipc/socket-server.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/typed-command-routing.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts\n=== spec 008 cold bounds ===\n3:description: \"Meaning matching needs a local Ollama server with nomic-embed-text, yet no install document, doctor route or brief tells a user who installs Skilled into their own repository that it exists, what it costs or that it is off. This phase makes the state visible, adds one doctor route that plans the setup and waits for a yes, writes the cost into the install documents from a committed measurement script and defines the absent, cold and slow cases with tests.\"\n32:| **Handoff Criteria** | `/doctor:setup` names the embedder state, `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` plans the setup and writes nothing without a yes, the install documents state the measured cost and the absent, model-missing, cold and slow tests pass |\n42:**Scope Boundary**: What a person who installs Skilled into their own repository sees and does about the embedder that meaning matching needs. The state, one doctor route, the install documents, a committed measurement script and the behaviour when the embedder is absent, missing its model, cold or slow. Scoring, the meaning bar, the lane weight and the embedder choice stay as they are.\n53:- A deadline on the prompt embedding and tests for the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n65:A user who installs Skilled can see whether meaning matching is on, set it up through one doctor route that shows its cost before it acts, read that cost in the install documents and keep a working advisor when the embedder is absent, cold or slow.\n105:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:143:export const DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500;\n132:The operator's own first reading on the same Mac, reported in the dispatch brief and not rerun here because it needs the model unloaded: `ollama serve` idle at 46 MB resident, 421 MB in total with the model loaded, cold embedding calls of 271 to 277 ms over 3 calls and one advisor CLI call of 413 ms with the model cold. The phase replaces this reading with the output of the committed script (REQ-001).\n159:- **Model cold.** Nothing preloads the model. The first prompt after 5 idle minutes pays the load inside the 5,000 ms query deadline.\n160:- **Slow call.** The query deadline is `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000` (`system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts:110`), overridden only by `OLLAMA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` (`:124`). The Claude hook passes a budget of `DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500` (`hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:143`) and `.claude/settings.json:150` gives the hook 3 seconds. When the CLI child runs past its budget, `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` returns its fail-open result with reason `timeout` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:559`). So a server that accepts the connection and never answers costs the whole brief, not only meaning matching. This is read from the code and not reproduced, because reproducing it needs a hung server.\n172:- Commit `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, which records the model size, the resident memory of the server and its model runner, the loaded size, the keep-alive expiry, warm and cold embedding latency and advisor CLI latency as one JSON object. Without it no number in an install document can be reproduced.\n176:- Bound the prompt embedding with its own deadline of 750 ms, give a missing model and a timeout their own `disabledReason`, add a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning to a recommendation that ran without a prompt vector and test the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n211:| `ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` | Create | Absent, model-missing, cold, slow and warning cases |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '100,130p' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts; echo \\\"=== 250 fallback callers ===\\\"; grep -rln \\\"skill-advisor-cli-fallback\\\" .skilled --include=*.ts | grep -v node_modules | head -6; echo \\\"=== spec 008 cold bounds ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"cold\\\\|271\\\\|277\\\\|2500\\\\|5000\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802532859,"end":1794802537300}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794802538453,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","part":{"id":"prt_1e29157d5001gOgQPv68CrNezG","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","messageID":"msg_1e2912a6e001nFjG6290gBo07f","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"d835894c32ac890cbd87de02cb826475ef99d87c","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":627,"output":197,"reasoning":189,"cache":{"read":217344,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794802540665,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","part":{"id":"prt_1e2916079001NhUPdJlYqRm4kQ","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","messageID":"msg_1e29157da001KbjxdkzKl3Eliz","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d835894c32ac890cbd87de02cb826475ef99d87c"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802565017,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2918091001gVw2aRkaeP20hd","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffeT6EyjaVEb2SkHU","messageID":"msg_1e29157da001KbjxdkzKl3Eliz","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a23e7e4c588a3a25","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: The cold first prompt — measured load versus waiting bounds\n\n## Focus\n\nBound the cold first prompt on the built state. Iteration 4 established that live organic rows are mostly cache hits, and iteration 3 established that the fail-open path records no elapsed time, so the cold path is exactly the path neither instrument can price. This pass reads the phase 008 measurement, the cascade probe default, the CLI's cold wait and the hook budget and composes them into one chain.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the phase 008 committed measurement for the cold embedding and cold CLI calls.\n2. Read the cascade probe default, the CLI cold-start wait, the local-scorer deadline and the Claude hook timeout in the current code.\n3. Composed the worst-case cold chain per bound and compared it with the measured cold work.\n4. Re-read the `unavailable` population in the health records to see what the instrument records for a cold failure.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The measured cold work is about 690 ms: 271-277 ms for a cold embedding call plus 413 ms for the advisor CLI with the model cold.** Against the 2,500 ms Claude hook budget that is 27.6 percent, so a cold first prompt does not by itself exhaust the budget. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:132]\n\n2. **The cascade probe's default 2,500 ms can consume the whole hook child budget before any scoring work starts.** `SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS` defaults to 2,500 ms inside `auto-select.ts`, while the Claude shim kills its child at 2,500 ms. A probe that runs to its default therefore leaves zero time for the CLI, and the failure mode is a fail-open brief, not a slow brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts:116-119] [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:160]\n\n3. **Both cold waits on the server side are twice the caller's budget.** The CLI waits up to 5,000 ms for a cold daemon (`COLD_START_WAIT_MS`), and the local scorer has a 5,000 ms deadline (`LOCAL_SCORER_TIMEOUT_MS`); the hook that called them gives up at 2,500 ms. A path that honours its own 5 s wait can only ever be observed from the caller as a timeout. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:33-36] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:43-45]\n\n4. **The production record prices the cold failure at zero.** The 664 `unavailable` rows have p50 0 ms and p95 2 ms, so a cold first prompt that fails open contributes the cheapest possible row to every aggregate; the population that should carry the cold cost carries none of it. [SOURCE: $TMPDIR/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl]\n\n5. **What would confirm the bound: one sandbox cold start with the model unloaded.** Unload the embed model, wait past its five-minute keep-alive, run one prompt through the real hook and record wall time, the cascade probe's own duration and the fail-open reason. Absent that, 690 ms is measured work and 2,500 ms is a waiting bound, not a first-prompt cost. [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-4]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reading a cold first-prompt cost from the health records: the fail-open branch writes 0 ms, so the record cannot carry it.\n- Treating 2,500 ms as the cold cost: it is the cascade probe's ceiling, and the measured cold work is 690 ms.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- The phase 008 committed cost script needs the model unloaded to reproduce the cold numbers, and unloading is a process action this read-only lane may not take.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none.\n- Contradictory evidence: the measured cold work (690 ms) and the 2,500 ms probe default describe different things and are not in conflict; the second is a bound on the first.\n- Missing dependencies: no cold-start run was possible; recorded as an inference with its confirming test.\n- Partial success: all four actions produced evidence; the cold number stays an inference. Status `complete`.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:132, 159-160`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts:116-119`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:33-45`\n- `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:160`\n- `$TMPDIR/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.70\n- Questions addressed: KQ5's cold-path half (which path the instrument misses)\n- Questions answered: none new; this prices a path the answered question named\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: composing the bounds from four files produced a sharper claim than any one file — the risk is a probe ceiling, not the model load, and that reorders what a fix should target.\n- What did not work and why: no committed artifact records a cold hook wall time, so the composition remains an inference.\n- What I would do differently: look for the cascade probe's own timing record before composing bounds; if one exists it would replace the inference.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 6: measure per-session brief cost. The directive-lifecycle dedup drops the 219-byte directive after the first proven repeat, so the 270.6-byte mean is not what a session pays per prompt. Count head-only versus full briefs from the organic `emittedBytes` distribution and read the dedup gate.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: The cold first prompt — measured load versus waiting bounds\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nBound the cold first prompt on the built state. Iteration 4 established that live organic rows are mostly cache hits, and iteration 3 established that the fail-open path records no elapsed time, so the cold path is exactly the path neither instrument can price. This pass reads the phase 008 measurement, the cascade probe default, the CLI's cold wait and the hook budget and composes them into one chain.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the phase 008 committed measurement for the cold embedding and cold CLI calls.\\n2. Read the cascade probe default, the CLI cold-start wait, the local-scorer deadline and the Claude hook timeout in the current code.\\n3. Composed the worst-case cold chain per bound and compared it with the measured cold work.\\n4. Re-read the `unavailable` population in the health records to see what the instrument records for a cold failure.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The measured cold work is about 690 ms: 271-277 ms for a cold embedding call plus 413 ms for the advisor CLI with the model cold.** Against the 2,500 ms Claude hook budget that is 27.6 percent, so a cold first prompt does not by itself exhaust the budget. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:132]\\n\\n2. **The cascade probe's default 2,500 ms can consume the whole hook child budget before any scoring work starts.** `SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS` defaults to 2,500 ms inside `auto-select.ts`, while the Claude shim kills its child at 2,500 ms. A probe that runs to its default therefore leaves zero time for the CLI, and the failure mode is a fail-open brief, not a slow brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts:116-119] [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:160]\\n\\n3. **Both cold waits on the server side are twice the caller's budget.** The CLI waits up to 5,000 ms for a cold daemon (`COLD_START_WAIT_MS`), and the local scorer has a 5,000 ms deadline (`LOCAL_SCORER_TIMEOUT_MS`); the hook that called them gives up at 2,500 ms. A path that honours its own 5 s wait can only ever be observed from the caller as a timeout. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:33-36] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:43-45]\\n\\n4. **The production record prices the cold failure at zero.** The 664 `unavailable` rows have p50 0 ms and p95 2 ms, so a cold first prompt that fails open contributes the cheapest possible row to every aggregate; the population that should carry the cold cost carries none of it. [SOURCE: $TMPDIR/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl]\\n\\n5. **What would confirm the bound: one sandbox cold start with the model unloaded.** Unload the embed model, wait past its five-minute keep-alive, run one prompt through the real hook and record wall time, the cascade probe's own duration and the fail-open reason. Absent that, 690 ms is measured work and 2,500 ms is a waiting bound, not a first-prompt cost. [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-4]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Reading a cold first-prompt cost from the health records: the fail-open branch writes 0 ms, so the record cannot carry it.\\n- Treating 2,500 ms as the cold cost: it is the cascade probe's ceiling, and the measured cold work is 690 ms.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- The phase 008 committed cost script needs the model unloaded to reproduce the cold numbers, and unloading is a process action this read-only lane may not take.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: none.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the measured cold work (690 ms) and the 2,500 ms probe default describe different things and are not in conflict; the second is a bound on the first.\\n- Missing dependencies: no cold-start run was possible; recorded as an inference with its confirming test.\\n- Partial success: all four actions produced evidence; the cold number stays an inference. Status `complete`.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:132, 159-160`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts:116-119`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:33-45`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:160`\\n- `$TMPDIR/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.70\\n- Questions addressed: KQ5's cold-path half (which path the instrument misses)\\n- Questions answered: none new; this prices a path the answered question named\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: composing the bounds from four files produced a sharper claim than any one file — the risk is a probe ceiling, not the model load, and that reorders what a fix should target.\\n- What did not work and why: no committed artifact records a cold hook wall time, so the composition remains an inference.\\n- What I would do differently: look for the cascade probe's own timing record before composing bounds; if one exists it would replace the inference.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nIteration 6: measure per-session brief cost. The directive-lifecycle dedup drops the 219-byte directive after the first proven repeat, so the 270.6-byte mean is not what a session pays per prompt. Count head-only versus full briefs from the organic `emittedBytes` distribution and read the dedup gate.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance-5/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802548881,"end":1794802565017}}}}
